@startuml sequence_forecast
skinparam backgroundColor #F5F5F5

participant "MongoDB" as db
participant "LSTM Service\n(Forecasting)" as lstm_svc
participant "Data\nProcessor" as processor
participant "LSTM\nModel" as lstm_model
participant "Post\nProcessor" as post
participant "MongoDB" as db2

db -> lstm_svc: Get price_history (5-7 days)
activate lstm_svc
activate db
db --> lstm_svc: Prices array with dates
deactivate db

lstm_svc -> processor: Raw price data
activate processor

processor -> processor: Data Cleaning:
note right
- Remove null/NaN values
- Handle missing dates
- Remove statistical outliers
  (Z-score > 3)
- Interpolate missing values
end note

processor -> processor: Data Normalization
note right
Using StandardScaler fitted on
training data:
normalized = (price - mean) / std
end note

processor -> processor: Sequence Preparation
note right
Given prices: [p0, p1, p2, p3, p4, p5, p6]
Create sequence for LSTM:
X = [p0, p1, p2, p3, p4]  (look_back=5)
y = p5  (predict p5)
X is reshaped to (1, 5, 1)
end note

processor --> lstm_svc: Normalized sequence
deactivate processor

lstm_svc -> lstm_model: Forward pass
activate lstm_model

note right
Architecture:
Input: (batch=1, seq_len=5, features=1)
  ↓
LSTM(128 units, dropout=0.2)
  ↓
LSTM(64 units, dropout=0.2)
  ↓
Dense(32, ReLU)
  ↓
Output Dense(1, Linear)
  ↓
Raw prediction (normalized)
end note

lstm_model --> lstm_svc: Normalized forecast
deactivate lstm_model

lstm_svc -> post: Post-processing
activate post

post -> post: Inverse Normalization
note right
actual_forecast = 
  (normalized_forecast * std) + mean
end note

post -> post: Calculate Metrics
note right
Compare forecast with recent
actual prices to get:
- MAE (Mean Absolute Error)
- RMSE (Root Mean Squared Error)
- MAPE (Mean Absolute 
  Percentage Error)
end note

post -> post: Determine Direction
note right
price_change = 
  (forecast - current) / current * 100%

IF change >= 5%: "UP_SHARP" ⬆
IF 1% <= change < 5%: "UP_MILD" ↗
IF -1% < change < 1%: "STABLE" ↔
IF -5% < change <= -1%: "DOWN_MILD" ↘
IF change <= -5%: "DOWN_SHARP" ⬇
end note

post --> lstm_svc: Forecast result object
deactivate post

lstm_svc -> db2: Save forecast_results
activate db2
note right
{
  product_id: ObjectId,
  forecast_date: ISODate,
  forecast_price: 15,500,000,
  actual_price: 15,200,000,
  mae: 450,000,
  mape: 2.8,
  direction: "UP_MILD",
  confidence: 0.78,
  look_back_days: 5
}
end note

db2 --> lstm_svc: Acknowledged
deactivate db2

lstm_svc -> db2: Trigger Recommendation Engine
activate db2
note right
Combine:
- forecast_direction
- current_price vs avg_price
- product_quality_score (PQS)

→ Generate recommendation
end note

db2 --> lstm_svc: Recommendation saved
deactivate db2

lstm_svc --> lstm_svc: Forecasting complete
deactivate lstm_svc

@enduml
